description:
# FakePlayer-PNX
Spawn and control fake players on PowerNukkitX 3.0.0.

Inspired by [Muqsit/FakePlayer](https://github.com/Muqsit/FakePlayer) for PocketMine-MP.

## Installation
PowerNukkitX 3.0.0 and Java 21 are required.

When launching the PNX JAR directly, keep its Java 21 module-opening option:
`--add-opens=java.base/java.lang=ALL-UNNAMED`.

Place `FakePlayer-PNX.jar` in your server's `plugins/` folder and restart.

On first run, a `players.json` file is created in the plugin data folder. Add entries to spawn fake players automatically at startup.

## players.json
```jsonc
{
  "uuid-v4-string": {
    "xuid": "required",
    "gamertag": "required",
    "behaviours": {
      "fakeplayerpnx:pvp": {},
      "fakeplayerpnx:auto_equip_armor": {}
    }
  }
}
```

## Commands
| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `/fp list` | List all online fake players |
| `/fp tpall` | Teleport all fake players to your position |
| `/fp chat <name> <message>` | Make a fake player send a chat message |
| `/fp interact <name>` | Make a fake player interact with the block they are looking at |

**Permission:** `fakeplayerpnx.command` (default: op)

## Built-in Behaviours

### `fakeplayerpnx:pvp`
Makes the fake player hunt and attack the nearest living entity (except creative-mode players).

| Config key | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `reach_distance` | `4.0` | Attack reach in blocks |
| `pvp_idle_time` | `500` | Ticks without movement before teleporting back to spawn |

### `fakeplayerpnx:auto_equip_armor`
Automatically equips any armor piece the fake player picks up.

## API

### Spawning a fake player
```java
FakePlayerPlugin plugin = FakePlayerPlugin.getInstance();

FakePlayerInfo info = FakePlayerInfoBuilder.create()
        .setUsername("MyBot")
        .setXuid("0")
        .setUuid("xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx")
        .setSkin(/* optional Skin */)
        .addBehaviour("fakeplayerpnx:pvp", Map.of("reach_distance", 4.0))
        .build();

FakePlayer fakePlayer = plugin.getHandler().addPlayer(info);
```

### Checking if a player is a fake player
```java
FakePlayerHandler handler = FakePlayerPlugin.getInstance().getHandler();
boolean isFake = handler.isFakePlayer(player);
```

### Removing a fake player
```java
handler.removePlayer(player);
// or by UUID:
handler.removePlayer(uuid);
```

### Listeners
```java
handler.addListener(new FakePlayerListener() {
    @Override
    public void onPlayerAdd(FakePlayer fp) {
        // fake player joined
    }

    @Override
    public void onPlayerRemove(FakePlayer fp) {
        // fake player removed
    }
});
```

### Registering a custom behaviour
```java
handler.getBehaviourFactory().register("myplugin:my_behaviour", (config) -> new MyBehaviour(config));
```

Custom behaviours implement `FakePlayerBehaviour`:
```java
public class MyBehaviour implements FakePlayerBehaviour {

    @Override
    public void onAddToPlayer(FakePlayer fakePlayer) {}

    @Override
    public void tick(FakePlayer fakePlayer) {
        // runs every server tick
    }

    @Override
    public void onRemoveFromPlayer(FakePlayer fakePlayer) {}
}
```
